# Archive line-ending policy.
#
# Publisher ownership records the SHA-256 of WORKING-TREE bytes, so the bytes a
# checkout produces must be deterministic and identical on every machine. Left
# to each developer's global core.autocrlf, the same commit could check out as
# LF on one machine and CRLF on another, and every recorded checksum would be
# wrong on one of them.
#
# CRLF is chosen because it matches the archive's existing published reports,
# whose recorded checksums were taken from CRLF working-tree bytes.
#
# Every OWNED text file needs an explicit rule here. A rule is not optional
# tidiness: an owned file with no rule falls back to the ambient core.autocrlf,
# which is exactly the non-determinism this file exists to remove.
*.html text eol=crlf
*.js   text eol=crlf
*.css  text eol=crlf
*.json text eol=crlf
*.svg  text eol=crlf

# This file is itself owned and checksummed, so it must pin its own endings.
.gitattributes text eol=crlf

# Binary formats must never be line-ending converted or diffed as text.
*.xlsx binary
*.png  binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
